    title: "Why it matters",
    body:
        "The shuffle swings the eighths: each beat is a triplet with the middle note left out, long-short, long-short. It is the bounce of blues, boogie and roadhouse rock, and a straight drummer sounds stiff the moment the band starts to shuffle.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "How to play it",
    body:
        "Right hand on the hi-hat plays the first and third note of every triplet, never the middle. Snare on 2 and 4 on the first triplet note, kick on 1 and 3. Keep the short note light so the long one carries.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "Practice tips",
    body:
        "Count \"1-trip-let, 2-trip-let\" and only play \"1\" and \"let\". Line 3 doubles the kick into the shuffle rhythm, line 4 adds a ghost on the \"let\" of 3, line 6 moves the right hand to the ride while the foot closes the hi-hat on 2 and 4.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "Where you hear it",
    body:
        "Stevie Ray Vaughan \"Pride and Joy\" with Chris Layton, ZZ Top \"La Grange\" with Frank Beard, early Fleetwood Mac blues records and every twelve-bar blues jam.",
  ),
];
